# /etc/fw_env.config — where fw_printenv / fw_setenv find the U-Boot environment.
#
# MUST mirror the U-Boot persistent-env location set by the kernel-side fragment
# meta-rockchip-rk3506/recipes-bsp/u-boot/files/rk3506-env-mmc.config:
#   CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET = 0xC00000  (12 MiB into the eMMC user area)
#   CONFIG_ENV_SIZE   = 0x8000    (32 KiB)
# Env lives in the 8-16 MiB loader gap on mmcblk0 (clear of u-boot.img @8 MiB and
# the boot partition @16 MiB). This is the OTA A/B slot state — see OTA_SWUPDATE_PLAN.md.
#
# Single env copy for M1 (no redundant copy yet — see plan). If a redundant env is
# added later, add a second line at its offset.
#
# <device>      <offset>    <env size>  <sector size (eMMC = 512B)>
/dev/mmcblk0    0xC00000    0x8000      0x200
